        <mxCell id="c52" value="&lt;i&gt;Fiscal 2026, to one scale. An exposure is the amount of the documents that failed a control, not a misstatement. Counted together, D1 and D2 (D2 is the 69 credits whose approver also applied the invoice&#x27;s cash, 68,514.82) would add to 240,822.22, which reaches materiality; counted once, the 172 credits that fail either test are 197,278.32, between performance materiality and materiality. The refund patterns stay between the clearly trivial threshold and performance materiality, while the year&#x27;s 222 credits, 260,457.72, are the potential magnitude of the credit patterns: a rating rests on likelihood, magnitude and compensating controls, not on how many exceptions a test finds.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="486" width="860" height="83" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
